['name'=>'String Formatting','brief'=>'sprintf, concatenation, interpolation','explanation':'String interpolation embeds variables in double-quoted strings. Concatenation (.) joins strings. sprintf() provides printf-style formatting.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Interpolation</span>\n<span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">\'John\'</span>;\n<span class="var">$s</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Hello, </span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="str">!"</span>;\n<span class="var">$s</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Hello, </span><span class="op">{</span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="op">}</span><span class="str">!"</span>;\n<span class="cmt">// Concatenation</span>\n<span class="var">$s</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Hello"</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">", "</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"!"</span>;\n<span class="cmt">// sprintf</span>\n<span class="var">$s</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">sprintf</span>(<span class="str">"Price: $%.2f"</span>, <span class="num">19.99</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">\'Alice\'</span>;\n<span class="var">$age</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="num">28</span>;\n<span class="var">$price</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="num">19.99</span>;\n\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"</span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="str"> is </span><span class="var">$age</span><span class="str"> years old&lt;br&gt;"</span>;\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"</span><span class="op">{</span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="op">}</span><span class="str"> costs </span><span class="op">{</span><span class="var">$price</span><span class="op">}</span><span class="str">&lt;br&gt;"</span>;\n\n<span class="var">$s</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Hello"</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">", "</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"!"</span>;\n\n<span class="var">$formatted</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">sprintf</span>(\n    <span class="str">"Price: $%.2f (ID: %04d)"</span>,\n    <span class="var">$price</span>, <span class="num">42</span>\n);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$formatted</span>;\n<span class="cmt">// Price: $19.99 (ID: 0042)</span>','useCases'=>['Building dynamic messages','Formatting currency/numbers','Creating SQL queries safely','Log message formatting'],'mistakes'=>['Using single quotes prevents interpolation','Not escaping special chars in sprintf','Mixing concatenation and interpolation'],['tips'=>['Use double quotes for interpolation','sprintf for number formatting','{} for complex variable expressions'],'interview'=>['sprintf vs printf?','Single vs double quotes?','Named arguments in sprintf?']],
['name'=>'Split & Join','brief'=>'Explode, implode, preg_split','explanation':'explode() splits a string into an array by delimiter. implode/join joins array elements. preg_split() uses regex for complex splitting. str_word_count() counts words.','syntax'=>'<span class="fn">explode</span>(<span class="str">\', \'</span>, <span class="var">$csv</span>);\n<span class="fn">implode</span>(<span class="str">\', \'</span>, <span class="var">$arr</span>);\n<span class="fn">preg_split</span>(<span class="str">\'/\\s+\'</span>, <span class="var">$str</span>);\n<span class="fn">str_word_count</span>(<span class="var">$str</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$csv</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"apple,banana,cherry"</span>;\n<span class="var">$fruits</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">explode</span>(<span class="str">\', \'</span>, <span class="var">$csv</span>);\n<span class="fn">print_r</span>(<span class="var">$fruits</span>);\n<span class="cmt">// [apple, banana, cherry]</span>\n\n<span class="var">$result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">implode</span>(<span class="str">\' | \'</span>, <span class="var">$fruits</span>);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$result</span>;\n<span class="cmt">// apple | banana | cherry</span>\n\n<span class="var">$sentence</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Hello   World   PHP"</span>;\n<span class="var">$words</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">preg_split</span>(<span class="str">\'/\\s+\'</span>, <span class="var">$sentence</span>);\n<span class="fn">print_r</span>(<span class="var">$words</span>);\n<span class="cmt">// [Hello, World, PHP]</span>\n\n<span class="var">$text</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Hello World"</span>;\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">str_word_count</span>(<span class="var">$text</span>); <span class="cmt">// 2</span>\n<span 