'id'=>'functions','name'=>'Functions','icon'=>'🎯','color'=>'#ef4444',
'subs'=>[
['name'=>'Function Basics','brief'=>'Declaring and calling functions','explanation':'Functions are reusable blocks of code declared with function keyword. They can accept parameters and return values. Functions are first-class in PHP and can be stored in variables.','syntax'=>'<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">greet</span>(<span class="var">$name</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">"Hello, </span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="str">!"</span>;\n}\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">greet</span>(<span class="str">\'John\'</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Type declarations</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">add</span>(<span class="kw">int</span> <span class="var">$a</span>, <span class="kw">int</span> <span class="var">$b</span>): <span class="kw">int</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$a</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="var">$b</span>;\n}','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">greet</span>(<span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$name</span>): <span class="var">string</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">"Hello, </span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="str">!"</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">add</span>(<span class="kw">int</span> <span class="var">$a</span>, <span class="kw">int</span> <span class="var">$b</span>): <span class="kw">int</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$a</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="var">$b</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">divide</span>(<span class="kw">float</span> <span class="var">$a</span>, <span class="kw">float</span> <span class="var">$b</span>): <span class="op">?</span><span class="kw">float</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$b</span> <span class="op">!=</span> <span class="num">0</span> <span class="op">?</span> <span class="var">$a</span> <span class="op">/</span> <span class="var">$b</span> <span class="op">:</span> <span class="kw">null</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">greet</span>(<span class="str">"Alice"</span>);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">add</span>(<span class="num">5</span>, <span class="num">3</span>);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">divide</span>(<span class="num">10</span>, <span class="num">3</span>);','useCases'=>['Code reuse and DRY principle','Organizing code into modules','Creating reusable libraries','Building APIs and interfaces'],'mistakes'=>['Missing return statement','Not declaring types','Function name conflicts'],['tips'=>['Always declare parameter/return types','Use meaningful function names','Keep functions small and focused'],'interview'=>['What are first-class functions?','Named vs positional arguments?','How to declare nullable return type?']],
['name'=>'Parameters','brief'=>'Default, variadic, named args','explanation':'Parameters can have default values, be passed by reference, use variadic (...args), or named arguments (PHP 8). Named arguments allow skipping optional parameters.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Default value</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">greet</span>(<span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">\'Guest\'</span>) {}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Variadic</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">sum</span>(<span class="op">...</span><span class="var">$nums</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">array_sum</span>(<span class="var">$nums</span>);\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// By reference</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">inc</span>(<span class="op">&</span><span class="var">$val</span>) {\n    <span class="var">$val</span>++;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Named args (PHP 8)</span>\n<span class="fn">greet</span>(<span class="var">name</span>: <span class="str">\'John\'</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">createUser</span>(\n    <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$name</span>,\n    <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$email</span>,\n    <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$role</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">\'user\'</span>,\n    <span class="kw">bool</span> <span class="var">$active</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">true</span>\n): <span class="var">array</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">compact</span>(<span class="str">\'name\'</span>, <span class="str">\'email\'</span>, <span class="str">\'role\'</span>, <span class="str">\'active\'</span>);\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Default params</span>\n<span class="var">$u1</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">createUser</span>(<span class="str">"Alice"</span>, <span class="str">"a@b.com"</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Named args (PHP 8)</span>\n<span class="var">$u2</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">createUser</span>(\n    <span class="var">name</span>: <span class="str">"Bob"</span>,\n    <span class="var">email</span>: <span class="str">"b@b.com"</span>,\n    <span class="var">role</span>: <span class="str">"admin"</span>\n);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Variadic</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">log</span>(<span class="op">...</span><span class="var">$msgs</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="var">$msgs</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="var">$m</span>) <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$m</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"\n"</span>;\n}\n<span class="fn">log</span>(<span class="str">"a"</span>, <span class="str">"b"</span>, <span class="str">"c"</span>);','useCases'=>['Creating flexible APIs','Configuration with sensible defaults','Working with variable input counts','Improving code readability with named args'],'mistakes'=>['Mixing required and default params wrong','Not handling null variadic args','Ordering default params after required'],['tips'=>['Required params must come first','Use named args for clarity in calls','PHP 8 named args skip optional params'],'interview'=>['How do default parameters work?','What are named arguments in PHP 8?','How to create variadic functions?']],
['name'=>'Arrow Functions','brief'=>'Concise one-line functions (PHP 7.4)','explanation'=>'Arrow functions provide a concise syntax for single-expression functions. They automatically capture variables from the parent scope (unlike regular functions).','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Arrow function</span>\n<span class="var">$fn</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$x</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$x</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="num">2</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// With multiple params</span>\n<span class="var">$add</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$a</span>, <span class="var">$b</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$a</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="var">$b</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Auto-captures $tax</span>\n<span class="var">$tax</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="num">0.1</span>;\n<span class="var">$calc</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$price</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$price</span> <span class="op">*</span> (<span class="num">1</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="var">$tax</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$numbers</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="num">1</span>, <span class="num">2</span>, <span class="num">3</span>, <span class="num">4</span>, <span class="num">5</span>];\n\n<span class="cmt">// Map with arrow function</span>\n<span class="var">$doubled</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">array_map</span>(\n    <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$n</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="num">2</span>,\n    <span class="var">$numbers</span>\n);\n<span class="fn">print_r</span>(<span class="var">$doubled</span>);\n<span class="cmt">// [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// Filter with arrow function</span>\n<span class="var">$evens</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">array_filter</span>(\n    <span class="var">$numbers</span>,\n    <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$n</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">%</span> <span class="num">2</span> <span class="op">==</span> <span class="num">0</span>\n);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Auto-captures outer $rate</span>\n<span class="var">$rate</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="num">0.08</span>;\n<span class="var">$prices</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="num">100</span>, <span class="num">200</span>, <span class="num">300</span>];\n<span class="var">$withTax</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">array_map</span>(\n    <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$p</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$p</span> <span class="op">*</span> (<span class="num">1</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="var">$rate</span>),\n    <span class="var">$prices</span>\n);\n<span class="fn">print_r</span>(<span class="var">$withTax</span>);\n<span class="cmt">// [108, 216, 324]</span>','useCases'=>['Callback functions in array_map/filter','Short transformation logic','Sorting comparisons','Event handlers'],'mistakes'=>['Trying multi-line logic (use regular fn)','Not knowing they auto-capture scope','Confusing with regular closures'],tips=['Use arrow functions for short callbacks','They auto-capture parent scope variables','Use regular functions for complex logic'],'interview'=>['Arrow fn vs regular fn?','How does variable capture work?','When to use arrow vs closure?']],
['name'=>'Closures','brief'=>'Anonymous functions and binding','explanation':'Closures are anonymous functions that can capture variables from their enclosing scope. The Closure class provides bind() and call() methods. Used extensively in functional programming patterns.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Basic closure</span>\n<span class="var">$fn</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">function</span>(<span class="var">$x</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$x</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="num">2</span>;\n};\n\n<span class="cmt">// Use</span>\n<span class="fn">usort</span>(<span class="var">$arr</span>, <span class="kw">function</span>(<span class="var">$a</span>, <span class="var">$b</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$a</span> <span class="op">&lt;=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$b</span>;\n});\n\n<span class="cmt">// Bind</span>\n<span class="var">$closure</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">function</span>() {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$this</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="var">name</span>;\n};\n<span class="var">$bound</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$closure</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">bindTo</span>(<span class="var">$obj</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// Closure with use</span>\n<span class="var">$greeting</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Hello"</span>;\n<span class="var">$say</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">function</span>(<span class="var">$name</span>) <span class="kw">use</span> (<span class="op">&</span><span class="var">$greeting</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">"</span><span class="var">$greeting</span><span class="str">, </span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="str">!"</span>;\n};\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$say</span>(<span class="str">"Alice"</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Array callback</span>\n<span class="var">$numbers</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="num">5</span>, <span class="num">2</span>, <span class="num">8</span>, <span class="num">1</span>];\n<span class="fn">usort</span>(<span class="var">$numbers</span>, <span class="kw">function</span>(<span class="var">$a</span>, <span class="var">$b</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$a</span> <span class="op">&lt;=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$b</span>;\n});\n\n<span class="cmt">// Closure as parameter</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">process</span>(<span class="var">array</span> <span class="var">$data</span>, <span class="callable</span> <span class="var">$callback</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">array_map</span>(<span class="var">$callback</span>, <span class="var">$data</span>);\n}\n<span class="var">$result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">process</span>(\n    [<span class="num">1</span>,<span class="num">2</span>,<span class="num">3</span>],\n    <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$x</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$x</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="var">$x</span>\n);','useCases'=>['Callback functions in sorting/filtering','Functional programming patterns','Event handling','Strategy pattern implementation'],'mistakes'=>['Forgetting to use use keyword','Not passing by reference when needed','Overcomplicating simple callbacks'],['tips'=>['Use arrow functions instead when simple','use &var to pass by reference','Closures are first-class in PHP'],'interview'=>['What is a Closure in PHP?','How to capture variables with use?','Closure bind vs call?']]
]
];
$topics[] = [
'id'=>'logic','name'=>'Logic','icon'=>'🧠','color'=>'#64748b',
'subs'=>[
['name'=>'Algorithms','brief':'Sorting, searching, recursion','explanation':'Common algorithms in PHP include bubble sort, binary search, and recursion. Understanding algorithmic thinking helps solve complex problems efficiently. PHP arrays make many algorithms straightforward to implement.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Bubble sort</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">bubbleSort</span>(<span class="var">array</span> <span class="op">&</span><span class="var">$arr</span>): <span class="var">void</span> {\n    <span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">count</span>(<span class="var">$arr</span>);\n    <span class="kw">for</span> (<span class="var">$i</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="num">0</span>; <span class="var">$i</span><span class="op">&lt;</span><span class="var">$n</span>; <span class="var">$i</span><span class="op">++</span>)\n        <span class="kw">for</span> (<span class="var">$j</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="num">0</span>; <span class="var">$j</span><span class="op">&lt;</span><span class="var">$n</span><span class="op">-</span><span class="var">$i</span><span class="op">-</span><span class="num">1</span>; <span class="var">$j</span><span class="op">++</span>)\n            <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$j</span>]<span class="op">&gt;</span><span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$j</span><span class="op">+</span><span class="num">1</span>])\n                [<span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$j</span>],<span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$j</span><span class="op">+</span><span class="num">1</span>]]<span class="op">=</span>[<span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$j</span><span class="op">+</span><span class="num">1</span>],<span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$j</span>]];\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Binary search</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">binarySearch</span>(<span class="var">array</span> <span class="var">$arr</span>, <span class="var">$target</span>): <span class="var">int</span> {\n    <span class="var">$lo</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="num">0</span>; <span class="var">$hi</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="fn">count</span>(<span class="var">$arr</span>)<span class="op">-</span><span class="num">1</span>;\n    <span class="kw">while</span>(<span class="var">$lo</span><span class="op">&lt;=</span><span class="var">$hi</span>) {\n        <span class="var">$mid</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="fn">intdiv</span>(<span class="var">$lo</span><span class="op">+</span><span class="var">$hi</span>,<span class="num">2</span>);\n        <span class="kw">if</span>(<span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$mid</span>]<span class="op">==</span><span class="var">$target</span>) <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$mid</span>;\n        <span class="var">$arr</span>[<span class="var">$mid</span>]<span class="op">&lt;</span><span class="var">$target</span> <span class="op">?</span> <span class="var">$lo</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="var">$mid</span><span class="op">+</span><span class="num">1</span> <span class="op">:</span> <span class="var">$hi</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="var">$mid</span><span class="op">-</span><span class="num">1</span>;\n    }\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="op">-</span><span class="num">1</span>;\n}','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// Factorial using recursion</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">factorial</span>(<span class="kw">int</span> <span class="var">$n</span>): <span class="kw">int</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">&lt;=</span> <span class="num">1</span> <span class="op">?</span> <span class="num">1</span> <span class="op">:</span> <span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="fn">factorial</span>(<span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">-</span> <span class="num">1</span>);\n}\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">factorial</span>(<span class="num">5</span>); <span class="cmt">// 120</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// Fibonacci</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">fib</span>(<span class="kw">int</span> <span class="var">$n</span>): <span class="kw">int</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">&lt;=</span> <span class="num">1</span> <span class="op">?</span> <span class="var">$n</span> <span class="op">:</span> <span class="fn">fib</span>(<span class="var">$n</span><span class="op">-</span><span class="num">1</span>) <span class="op">+</span> <span class="fn">fib</span>(<span class="var">$n</span><span class="op">-</span><span class="num">2</span>);\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Find max in array</span>\n<span class="var">$nums</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="num">3</span>, <span class="num">7</span>, <span class="num">2</span>, <span class="num">9</span>, <span class="num">1</span>];\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">max</span>(<span class="var">$nums</span>); <span class="cmt">// 9</span>\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">min</span>(<span class="var">$nums</span>); <span class="cmt">// 1</span>','useCases'=>['Sorting custom data structures','Searching large datasets','Tree/graph traversal','Problem decomposition'],'mistakes'=>['Infinite recursion (missing base case)','Stack overflow with deep recursion','Inefficient O(n^2) solutions'],['tips'=>['Use PHP built-in sort/search when possible','Add base case for all recursive functions','Consider memoization for repeated calls'],'interview'=>['Explain recursion with an example?','What is time complexity?','How to optimize recursive functions?']],
['name'=>'Problem Solving','brief'=>'Decomposition and patterns','explanation':'Breaking problems into smaller parts is key. Common patterns: sliding window, two pointers, hash maps for lookups, divide and conquer. PHP arrays and built-in functions make many patterns easy.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Pattern: Validate array data</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">validate</span>(<span class="var">array</span> <span class="var">$data</span>): <span class="var">bool</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">array_reduce</span>(\n        <span class="var">$data</span>,\n        <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$ok</span>, <span class="var">$v</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$ok</span> <span class="op">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class="fn">isset</span>(<span class="var">$v</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>]),\n        <span class="kw">true</span>\n    );\n}","codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// Pattern: Flatten nested array</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">flatten</span>(<span class="var">array</span> <span class="var">$arr</span>): <span class="var">array</span> {\n    <span class="var">$result</span> <span class="op">=</span> [];\n    <span class="fn">array_walk_recursive</span>(<span class="var">$arr</span>, <span class="kw">fn</span>(<span class="var">$v</span>) <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$result</span>[] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$v</span>);\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$result</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Pattern: Group by key</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">groupBy</span>(<span class="var">array</span> <span class="var">$items</span>, <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$key</span>): <span class="var">array</span> {\n    <span class="var">$groups</span> <span class="op">=</span> [];\n    <span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="var">$items</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="var">$item</span>) {\n        <span class="var">$groups</span>[<span class="var">$item</span>[<span class="var">$key</span>]][] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$item</span>;\n    }\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$groups</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Pattern: Unique values</span>\n<span class="var">$data</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="num">1</span>,<span class="num">2</span>,<span class="num">2</span>,<span class="num">3</span>,<span class="num">3</span>,<span class="num">3</span>];\n<span class="var">$unique</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">array_unique</span>(<span class="var">$data</span>);','useCases'=>['Data transformation pipelines','Validation chains','Collection processing','Building report generators'],'mistakes'=>['Overcomplicating simple problems','Not using built-in array functions','Ignoring edge cases in solutions'],['tips'=>['Think before coding - plan approach','Use array_* functions for data operations','Test with edge cases (empty, single item)'],'interview'=>['How to approach coding problems?','What is algorithmic complexity?','Name common PHP array patterns']],
['name'=>'Validation','brief'=>'Input validation techniques','explanation':'Always validate and sanitize user input. Use filter_var/filter_input for standard validation. Custom validators for business rules. Never trust client-side validation alone.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Built-in filters</span>\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$email</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL</span>);\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$url</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_URL</span>);\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$ip</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_IP</span>);\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$int</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_INT</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Sanitization</span>\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$html</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_SANITIZE_FULL_SPECIAL_CHARS</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$email</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"user@example.com"</span>;\n\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$email</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL</span>)) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Valid email"</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="var">$age</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"25abc"</span>;\n<span class="var">$validAge</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">filter_var</span>(\n    <span class="var">$age</span>,\n    <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_INT</span>,\n    [<span class="str">"options"</span> <span class="op">=&gt;</span> [<span class="str">"min_range"</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="num">1</span>, <span class="str">"max_range"</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="num">120</span>]]\n);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$validAge</span> <span class="op">?</span> <span class="str">"Valid"</span> <span class="op">:</span> <span class="str">"Invalid"</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Custom validation</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">validatePassword</span>(<span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$p</span>): <span class="var">bool</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">strlen</span>(<span class="var">$p</span>) <span class="op">&gt;=</span> <span class="num">8</span>\n        <span class="op">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class="fn">preg_match</span>(<span class="str">\'/[A-Z]/\'</span>, <span class="var">$p</span>)\n        <span class="op">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class="fn">preg_match</span>(<span class="str">\'/[0-9]/\'</span>, <span class="var">$p</span>);\n}',['useCases'=>['Form input validation','API request validation','Email/URL verification','Password strength checking'],'mistakes'=>['Trusting client-side validation only','Not validating server-side','Using wrong filter type'],['tips'=>['Always validate server-side','Use built-in filter functions','Combine multiple validation rules'],'interview'=>['What is input validation?','How to validate email in PHP?','Why validate on server side?']]
]
];

$topics[] = [
'id'=>'files','name'=>'File Handling','icon'=>'📁','color'=>'#78716c',
'subs'=>[
['name'=>'File Read/Write','brief'=>'fopen, fread, fwrite, file_get_contents','explanation':'PHP provides multiple ways to read and write files. file_get_contents() and file_put_contents() are simplest. fopen/fread/fwrite offer more control. Always handle file errors gracefully.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Simple read/write</span>\n<span class="var">$content</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">file_get_contents</span>(<span class="str">\'file.txt\'</span>);\n<span class="fn">file_put_contents</span>(<span class="str">\'file.txt\'</span>, <span class="str">"data"</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Append</span>\n<span class="fn">file_put_contents</span>(<span class="str">\'log.txt\'</span>, <span class="str">"line\n"</span>, <span class="const">FILE_APPEND</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Advanced</span>\n<span class="var">$f</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">fopen</span>(<span class="str">\'file.txt\'</span>, <span class="str">\'r\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">fread</span>(<span class="var">$f</span>, <span class="fn">filesize</span>(<span class="str">\'file.txt\'</span>));\n<span class="fn">fclose</span>(<span class="var">$f</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// Write file</span>\n<span class="var">$data</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="str">\'name\'</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="str">\'Alice\'</span>, <span class="str">\'age\'</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="num">25</span>];\n<span class="fn">file_put_contents</span>(\n    <span class="str">\'user.json\'</span>,\n    <span class="fn">json_encode</span>(<span class="var">$data</span>, <span class="const">JSON_PRETTY_PRINT</span>)\n);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Read file</span>\n<span class="var">$json</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">file_get_contents</span>(<span class="str">\'user.json\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$user</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">json_decode</span>(<span class="var">$json</span>, <span class="kw">true</span>);\n<span class="fn">print_r</span>(<span class="var">$user</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Read line by line</span>\n<span class="var">$lines</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">file</span>(<span class="str">\'data.txt\'</span>, <span class="const">FILE_IGNORE_NEW_LINES</span>);\n<span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="var">$lines</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="var">$line</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$line</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"&lt;br&gt;"</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Check file exists</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">file_exists</span>(<span class="str">\'file.txt\'</span>)) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"File exists"</span>;\n}',['useCases'=>['Reading configuration files','Logging application events','Storing/retrieving JSON data','Processing CSV files'],'mistakes'=>['Not checking if file exists','Not handling fopen errors','Forgetting to fclose()'],['tips'=>['Use file_get_contents for simple reads','FILE_APPEND for logging','Always handle file operation errors'],'interview'=>['fopen modes explained?','file_get_contents vs fopen?','How to check file permissions?']],
['name'=>'File Upload','brief'=>'Handling file uploads securely','explanation':'File uploads use $_FILES superglobal. Always validate file type, size, and name. Move uploaded files with move_uploaded_file(). Never trust the client-provided filename.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// HTML form</span>\n<span class="cmt">// &lt;form method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data"&gt;</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// PHP handler</span>\n<span class="var">$file</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_FILES</span>[<span class="str">\'upload\'</span>];\n<span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">basename</span>(<span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>]);\n<span class="var">$type</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'type\'</span>];\n<span class="var">$size</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'size\'</span>];\n<span class="var">$tmp</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'tmp_name\'</span>];\n<span class="var">$err</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'error\'</span>];\n\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$err</span> <span class="op">===</span> <span class="const">UPLOAD_ERR_OK</span>) {\n    <span class="fn">move_uploaded_file</span>(<span class="var">$tmp</span>, <span class="str">"uploads/</span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="str">"</span>);\n}','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$_SERVER</span>[<span class="str">\'REQUEST_METHOD\'</span>] <span class="op">===</span> <span class="str">\'POST\'</span>) {\n    <span class="var">$file</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_FILES</span>[<span class="str">\'avatar\'</span>];\n\n    <span class="cmt">// Validate</span>\n    <span class="var">$allowed</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="str">\'image/jpeg\'</span>, <span class="str">\'image/png\'</span>];\n    <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">in_array</span>(<span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'type\'</span>], <span class="var">$allowed</span>)) {\n        <span class="kw">die</span>(<span class="str">"Invalid file type"</span>);\n    }\n    <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'size\'</span>] <span class="op">&gt;</span> <span class="num">5</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="num">1024</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="num">1024</span>) {\n        <span class="kw">die</span>(<span class="str">"File too large"</span>);\n    }\n\n    <span class="cmt">// Secure filename</span>\n    <span class="var">$ext</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">pathinfo</span>(<span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>], <span class="const">PATHINFO_EXTENSION</span>);\n    <span class="var">$newName</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">uniqid</span>(<span class="str">\'img_\'</span>) <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"."</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="var">$ext</span>;\n\n    <span class="fn">move_uploaded_file</span>(\n        <span class="var">$file</span>[<span class="str">\'tmp_name\'</span>],\n        <span class="str">"uploads/</span><span class="var">$newName</span><span class="str">"</span>\n    );\n}',['useCases'=>['User profile picture uploads','Document management systems','Import/Export functionality','Media library management'],'mistakes':['Not validating file type','Using original filename','Not checking upload errors'],'tips'=>['Use finfo_file for real MIME type','Generate unique filenames','Store uploads outside web root'],'interview'=>['How does PHP file upload work?','How to validate uploaded files?','move_uploaded_file security?']],
['name'=>'Directory Operations','brief'=>'Creating, scanning, deleting dirs','explanation':'PHP can create directories with mkdir(), list contents with scandir(), and delete with rmdir(). DirectoryIterator provides object-oriented directory traversal. Recursive operations with RecursiveDirectoryIterator.','syntax'=>'<span class="fn">mkdir</span>(<span class="str">\'new_dir\'</span>, <span class="num">0755</span>);\n<span class="fn">rmdir</span>(<span class="str">\'empty_dir\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$files</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">scandir</span>(<span class="str">\'uploads\'</span>);\n<span class="fn">unlink</span>(<span class="str">\'file.txt\'</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// Create directory</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">is_dir</span>(<span class="str">\'uploads\'</span>)) {\n    <span class="fn">mkdir</span>(<span class="str">\'uploads\'</span>, <span class="num">0755</span>, <span class="kw">true</span>);\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// List files</span>\n<span class="var">$files</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">scandir</span>(<span class="str">\'uploads\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$files</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">array_diff</span>(<span class="var">$files</span>, [<span class="str">\'.\'</span>, <span class="str">\'..\'</span>]);\n\n<span class="cmt">// File info</span>\n<span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="var">$files</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="var">$f</span>) {\n    <span class="var">$path</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"uploads/</span><span class="var">$f</span><span class="str">"</span>;\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"</span><span class="var">$f</span><span class="str">: "</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="fn">filesize</span>(<span class="var">$path</span>) <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">" bytes\n"</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Recursive list</span>\n<span class="var">$it</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">RecursiveIteratorIterator</span>(\n    <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">RecursiveDirectoryIterator</span>(<span class="str">\'src\'</span>)\n);\n<span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="var">$it</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="var">$file</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$file</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"\n"</span>;\n}','useCases'=>['Creating upload directories','Scanning folder contents','File management systems','Building file browsers'],'mistakes'=>['Not checking directory exists before mkdir','Using wrong permissions','Not handling empty directories'],['tips'=>['Use 0755 permissions for web dirs','array_diff to remove . and ..','RecursiveIterator for deep traversal'],'interview'=>['mkdir permissions explained?','How to list files in a directory?','Recursive directory traversal?']]
]
];
$topics[] = [
'id'=>'forms','name'=>'Forms','icon'=>'📋','color'=>'#0ea5e9',
'subs'=>[
['name'=>'GET vs POST','brief'=>'HTTP methods for forms','explanation':'GET appends data to URL (use for non-sensitive data, bookmarks). POST sends data in request body (use for sensitive/large data). $_GET and $_POST superglobals access the data.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// HTML</span>\n<span class="cmt">// &lt;form method="GET" action="process.php"&gt;</span>\n<span class="cmt">// &lt;form method="POST" action="process.php"&gt;</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// PHP</span>\n<span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_GET</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>;\n<span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>;','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$_SERVER</span>[<span class="str">\'REQUEST_METHOD\'</span>] <span class="op">===</span> <span class="str">\'POST\'</span>) {\n    <span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>;\n    <span class="var">$email</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'email\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>;\n\n    <span class="cmt">// Process form data</span>\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Name: </span><span class="var">$name</span><span class="str">&lt;br&gt;"</span>;\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Email: </span><span class="var">$email</span><span class="str">&lt;br&gt;"</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// GET parameter</span>\n<span class="var">$page</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_GET</span>[<span class="str">\'page\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="num">1</span>;\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Page: </span><span class="var">$page</span><span class="str">"</span>;','useCases'=>['User registration forms','Search forms (GET)','Contact forms (POST)','Login forms (POST)'],['mistakes'=>['Using GET for sensitive data','Not checking REQUEST_METHOD','Not using null coalescing'],['tips'=>['Use POST for mutations','Always validate server-side','Check REQUEST_METHOD first'],'interview'=>['When to use GET vs POST?','Why POST for passwords?','How to handle file uploads?']],
['name'=>'Form Validation','brief'=>'Server-side validation','explanation':'Always validate form data server-side. Use filter_var for standard validation. Custom validators for business rules. Return meaningful error messages to users.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Standard validation</span>\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$email</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL</span>);\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$url</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_URL</span>);\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$ip</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_IP</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Required check</span>\n<span class="fn">empty</span>(<span class="fn">trim</span>(<span class="var">$name</span>));','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$errors</span> <span class="op">=</span> [];\n<span class="var">$name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">trim</span>(<span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$email</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">trim</span>(<span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'email\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$age</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'age\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>;\n\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">empty</span>(<span class="var">$name</span>)) {\n    <span class="var">$errors</span>[] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Name is required"</span>;\n}\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$email</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL</span>)) {\n    <span class="var">$errors</span>[] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Invalid email"</span>;\n}\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$age</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_VALIDATE_INT</span>,\n    [<span class="str">"options"</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span>[<span class="str">"min_range"</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="num">1</span>,<span class="str">"max_range"</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="num">120</span>]])) {\n    <span class="var">$errors</span>[] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"Invalid age"</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">empty</span>(<span class="var">$errors</span>)) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Form is valid!"</span>;\n} else {\n    <span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="var">$errors</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="var">$e</span>) {\n        <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$e</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"&lt;br&gt;"</span>;\n    }\n}','useCases'=>['Registration form validation','Contact form processing','Search input sanitization','Profile update validation'],['mistakes'=>['Only validating client-side','Not trimming whitespace','Trusting $_POST data directly'],['tips'=>['Always trim input strings','Use filter_var for standard validation','Show errors near the fields'],'interview'=>['How to validate forms in PHP?','Why server-side validation?','Custom vs built-in validation?']],
['name'=>'Sanitization','brief'=>'Cleaning user input','explanation':'Sanitization removes or encodes potentially harmful characters. Use filter_var with sanitize filters. htmlspecialchars() prevents XSS. Never rely on client-side sanitization alone.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Sanitize filters</span>\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$html</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_SANITIZE_FULL_SPECIAL_CHARS</span>);\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$email</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_SANITIZE_EMAIL</span>);\n<span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$int</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_SANITIZE_NUMBER_INT</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// HTML escape</span>\n<span class="fn">htmlspecialchars</span>(<span class="var">$unsafe</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$unsafe</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"&lt;script&gt;alert(\'xss\')&lt;/script&gt;"</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Sanitize HTML</span>\n<span class="var">$safe</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">htmlspecialchars</span>(<span class="var">$unsafe</span>);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$safe</span>;\n<span class="cmt">// &lt;script&gt;alert(\'xss\')&lt;/script&gt;</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// Sanitize integers</span>\n<span class="var">$input</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"123abc"</span>;\n<span class="var">$clean</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$input</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_SANITIZE_NUMBER_INT</span>);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$clean</span>; <span class="cmt">// 123</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// Sanitize email</span>\n<span class="var">$email</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"user@exam&lt;b&gt;ple.com"</span>;\n<span class="var">$clean</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">filter_var</span>(<span class="var">$email</span>, <span class="const">FILTER_SANITIZE_EMAIL</span>);\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$clean</span>; <span class="cmt">// user@example.com</span>','useCases'=>['Preventing XSS attacks','Cleaning database input','Sanitizing file names','Processing user content'],['mistakes'=>['Forgetting htmlspecialchars on output','Using stripslashes unnecessarily','Not sanitizing before database queries'],['tips'=>['Sanitize on input, escape on output','htmlspecialchars for all HTML output','Use prepared statements for DB queries'],'interview'=>['Sanitization vs validation?','How to prevent XSS?','When to sanitize?']],
['name'=>'CSRF Protection','brief':'Cross-Site Request Forgery tokens','explanation':'CSRF attacks trick users into submitting unwanted forms. Protection uses unique tokens embedded in forms and verified on submission. Each session gets a unique token that must match on POST requests.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Generate token</span>\nsession_start();\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">isset</span>(<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>])) {\n    <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">bin2hex</span>(<span class="fn">random_bytes</span>(<span class="num">32</span>));\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// HTML form</span>\n<span class="cmt">// &lt;input type="hidden" name="csrf"</span>\n<span class="cmt">//        value="</span><span class="op">&lt;?=</span> <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>] <span class="op">?&gt;</span><span class="cmt">"&gt;</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// Verify</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>] <span class="op">!==</span> <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>]) {\n    <span class="kw">die</span>(<span class="str">"Invalid token"</span>);\n}','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\nsession_start();\n\n<span class="cmt">// Generate CSRF token</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">csrfToken</span>(): <span class="var">string</span> {\n    <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">isset</span>(<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>])) {\n        <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">bin2hex</span>(<span class="fn">random_bytes</span>(<span class="num">32</span>));\n    }\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>];\n}\n\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">verifyCsrf</span>(): <span class="var">bool</span> {\n    <span class="kw">return</span> (<span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>)\n        <span class="op">===</span> (<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'csrf\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>);\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// In form</span>\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"&lt;input type=\'hidden\' name=\'csrf\'</span>\n<span class="str">    value=\'"</span> <span class="op">.</span> <span class="fn">csrfToken</span>() <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"\'&gt;"</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// On submit</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">verifyCsrf</span>()) {\n    <span class="kw">die</span>(<span class="str">"CSRF token invalid"</span>);\n}','useCases'=>['Protecting form submissions','Securing AJAX POST requests','Preventing unauthorized state changes','Guarding against malicious links'],['mistakes'=>['Not using CSRF on state-changing requests','Regenerating token every request','Storing token in cookie'],['tips'=>['Use bin2hex(random_bytes(32))','Store token in session','Verify on every POST/PUT/DELETE'],'interview'=>['What is a CSRF attack?','How do CSRF tokens work?','Why use random_bytes()?']]
]
];

$topics[] = [
'id'=>'sessions','name'=>'Sessions & Cookies','icon'=>'🔐','color'=>'#d946ef',
'subs'=>[
['name'=>'Session Management','brief'=>'Server-side state storage','explanation':'Sessions store data on the server, identified by a session ID sent via cookie. Start with session_start(). Data stored in $_SESSION superglobal. Sessions persist across page loads until timeout or destruction.','syntax'=>'<span class="fn">session_start</span>();\n\n<span class="cmt">// Set session data</span>\n<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'user_id\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="num">42</span>;\n<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">\'John\'</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Get session data</span>\n<span class="var">$id</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'user_id\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="kw">null</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Destroy session</span>\n<span class="fn">session_unset</span>();\n<span class="fn">session_destroy</span>();','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\nsession_start();\n\n<span class="cmt">// Login</span>\n<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'user_id\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="num">42</span>;\n<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'role\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">\'admin\'</span>;\n<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'logged_in\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">true</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Check login</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'logged_in\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="kw">false</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Welcome back!"</span>;\n} <span class="kw">else</span> {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Please log in"</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Logout</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">logout</span>(): <span class="var">void</span> {\n    <span class="fn">session_unset</span>();\n    <span class="fn">session_destroy</span>();\n    <span class="fn">header</span>(<span class="str">\'Location: login.php\'</span>);\n    <span class="kw">exit</span>;\n}','useCases'=>['User authentication','Shopping cart persistence','Flash messages','Page visit tracking'],['mistakes'=>['Forgetting session_start()','Not using null coalescing','Not destroying session on logout'],['tips'=>['Call session_start() at top of page','Use session_regenerate_id() for security','Set session.cookie_httponly = 1'],'interview'=>['How do sessions work?','Session vs cookie security?','session_regenerate_id purpose?']],
['name'=>'Cookies','brief'=>'Client-side state storage','explanation':'Cookies store data on the client browser. Set with setcookie() before any output. Read from $_COOKIE. Have expiration, path, and domain settings. Limited to ~4KB per cookie.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Set cookie</span>\n<span class="fn">setcookie</span>(<span class="str">\'theme\'</span>, <span class="str">\'dark\'</span>, <span class="fn">time</span>() <span class="op">+</span> <span class="num">86400</span> <span class="op">*</span> <span class="num">30</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Read cookie</span>\n<span class="var">$theme</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_COOKIE</span>[<span class="str">\'theme\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'light\'</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Delete cookie</span>\n<span class="fn">setcookie</span>(<span class="str">\'theme\'</span>, <span class="str">\'\'</span>, <span class="fn">time</span>() <span class="op">-</span> <span class="num">3600</span>);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// Set cookies before any output</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span><span class="fn">isset</span>(<span class="var">$_COOKIE</span>[<span class="str">\'visits\'</span>])) {\n    <span class="fn">setcookie</span>(<span class="str">\'visits\'</span>, <span class="num">1</span>, <span class="fn">time</span>()<span class="op">+</span><span class="num">86400</span><span class="op">*</span><span class="num">365</span>);\n} <span class="kw">else</span> {\n    <span class="var">$count</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_COOKIE</span>[<span class="str">\'visits\'</span>] <span class="op">+</span> <span class="num">1</span>;\n    <span class="fn">setcookie</span>(<span class="str">\'visits\'</span>, <span class="var">$count</span>, <span class="fn">time</span>()<span class="op">+</span><span class="num">86400</span><span class="op">*</span><span class="num">365</span>);\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Theme preference</span>\n<span class="var">$theme</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_COOKIE</span>[<span class="str">\'theme\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'dark\'</span>;\n<span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Theme: </span><span class="var">$theme</span><span class="str">"</span>;\n\n<span class="cmt">// Remember form field</span>\n<span class="var">$email</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_COOKIE</span>[<span class="str">\'last_email\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="str">\'\'</span>;','useCases'=>['Remember user preferences','Track visitors without login','Store form draft data','Language/locale preference'],['mistakes'=>['Setting cookies after output','Not setting expiration','Using cookies for sensitive data'],['tips'=>['Set httponly flag for security','Use secure flag for HTTPS','Prefer sessions for sensitive data'],'interview'=>['Cookie vs session?','How to set secure cookies?','Cookie expiration handling?']],
['name'=>'Authentication','brief'=>'Login systems and access control','explanation':'Authentication verifies user identity. Use password_hash() and password_verify() for passwords. Store sessions for persistent login. Implement proper logout and session timeout.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// Register</span>\n<span class="var">$hash</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">password_hash</span>(<span class="var">$pass</span>, <span class="const">PASSWORD_DEFAULT</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Login</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">password_verify</span>(<span class="var">$input</span>, <span class="var">$hash</span>)) {\n    <span class="fn">session_start</span>();\n    <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'user_id\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$userId</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Check auth</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">requireAuth</span>(): <span class="var">void</span> {\n    <span class="fn">session_start</span>();\n    <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span>(<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'user_id\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="kw">false</span>)) {\n        <span class="fn">header</span>(<span class="str">\'Location: login.php\'</span>);\n        <span class="kw">exit</span>;\n    }\n}','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\nsession_start();\n\n<span class="cmt">// Register</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">register</span>(<span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$user</span>, <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$pass</span>): <span class="var">bool</span> {\n    <span class="var">$hash</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">password_hash</span>(<span class="var">$pass</span>, <span class="const">PASSWORD_DEFAULT</span>);\n    <span class="cmt">// Save $user and $hash to database</span>\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="kw">true</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Login</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">login</span>(<span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$user</span>, <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$pass</span>): <span class="var">bool</span> {\n    <span class="cmt">// Fetch hash from database</span>\n    <span class="var">$hash</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="cmt">/* from DB */</span>;\n    <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="fn">password_verify</span>(<span class="var">$pass</span>, <span class="var">$hash</span>)) {\n        <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'user_id\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="cmt">/* id */</span>;\n        <span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'logged_in\'</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">true</span>;\n        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="kw">true</span>;\n    }\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="kw">false</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="cmt">// Protect page</span>\n<span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="op">!</span>(<span class="var">$_SESSION</span>[<span class="str">\'logged_in\'</span>] <span class="op">??</span> <span class="kw">false</span>)) {\n    <span class="fn">header</span>(<span class="str">\'Location: login.php\'</span>);\n    <span class="kw">exit</span>;\n}',['useCases'=>['User login/registration','Admin panel access control','API authentication','Role-based access'],['mistakes'=>['Storing passwords in plain text','Not using password_hash/verify','Not regenerating session ID after login'],['tips'=>['Always use password_hash/verify','Regenerate session ID on login','Use HTTPS for production'],'interview'=>['How does password_hash work?','Session fixation prevention?','JWT vs sessions?']]
]
];

$topics[] = [
'id'=>'errors','name'=>'Error Handling','icon'=>'⚠️','color'=>'#f97316',
'subs'=>[
['name'=>'Error Types','brief'=>'Notice, Warning, Fatal, etc.','explanation':'PHP has several error levels: E_NOTICE (undefined vars), E_WARNING (non-fatal), E_ERROR (fatal), E_PARSE (syntax), E_DEPRECATED (outdated features). Configure error reporting with error_reporting() or php.ini.','syntax'=>'<span class="fn">error_reporting</span>(<span class="const">E_ALL</span>);\n<span class="fn">ini_set</span>(<span class="str">\'display_errors\'</span>, <span class="num">1</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Error levels</span>\n<span class="const">E_NOTICE</span>    <span class="cmt">// Minor issues</span>\n<span class="const">E_WARNING</span>   <span class="cmt">// Non-fatal</span>\n<span class="const">E_ERROR</span>     <span class="cmt">// Fatal</span>\n<span class="const">E_DEPRECATED</span><span class="cmt">// Outdated</span>','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// Set error reporting</span>\n<span class="fn">error_reporting</span>(<span class="const">E_ALL</span>);\n<span class="fn">ini_set</span>(<span class="str">\'display_errors\'</span>, <span class="num">1</span>);\n<span class="fn">ini_set</span>(<span class="str">\'log_errors\'</span>, <span class="num">1</span>);\n<span class="fn">ini_set</span>(<span class="str">\'error_log\'</span>, <span class="str">\'/var/log/php_errors.log\'</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Custom error handler</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">customError</span>(<span class="var">$errno</span>, <span class="var">$errstr</span>, <span class="var">$errfile</span>, <span class="var">$errline</span>) {\n    <span class="var">$msg</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="str">"</span><span class="var">$errstr</span><span class="str"> in </span><span class="var">$errfile</span><span class="str">:</span><span class="var">$errline</span><span class="str">\n"</span>;\n    <span class="fn">error_log</span>(<span class="var">$msg</span>);\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="kw">true</span>;\n}\n<span class="fn">set_error_handler</span>(<span class="str">\'customError\'</span>);\n\n<span class="cmt">// Trigger error</span>\n<span class="fn">trigger_error</span>(<span class="str">"Custom warning"</span>, <span class="const">E_USER_WARNING</span>);',['useCases'=>['Debugging during development','Production error logging','Custom error reporting','Application monitoring'],['mistakes'=>['Displaying errors in production','Not logging errors','Ignoring E_DEPRECATED warnings'],['tips'=>['Display in dev, log in production','Use try-catch for recoverable errors','Set custom error handler for logging'],'interview'=>['Error levels explained?','How to set custom error handler?','display_errors in production?']],
['name'=>'Try-Catch-Finally','brief'=>'Exception handling','explanation':'Exceptions are thrown with throw and caught with try-catch-finally. Exception is the base class. You can create custom exception classes. Finally block always executes regardless of exceptions.','syntax'=>'<span class="kw">try</span> {\n    <span class="cmt">// risky code</span>\n    <span class="kw">throw new</span> <span class="fn">Exception</span>(<span class="str">"Error"</span>);\n} <span class="kw">catch</span> (<span class="fn">Exception</span> <span class="var">$e</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$e</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">getMessage</span>();\n} <span class="kw">finally</span> {\n    <span class="cmt">// always runs</span>\n}","codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">divide</span>(<span class="kw">float</span> <span class="var">$a</span>, <span class="kw">float</span> <span class="var">$b</span>): <span class="kw">float</span> {\n    <span class="kw">if</span> (<span class="var">$b</span> <span class="op">==</span> <span class="num">0</span>) {\n        <span class="kw">throw new</span> <span class="fn">InvalidArgumentException</span>(\n            <span class="str">"Division by zero"</span>\n        );\n    }\n    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$a</span> <span class="op">/</span> <span class="var">$b</span>;\n}\n\n<span class="kw">try</span> {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="fn">divide</span>(<span class="num">10</span>, <span class="num">0</span>);\n} <span class="kw">catch</span> (<span class="fn">InvalidArgumentException</span> <span class="var">$e</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Error: </span><span class="var">$e-&gt;getMessage()</span><span class="str">"</span>;\n} <span class="kw">finally</span> {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"&lt;br&gt;Cleanup done"</span>;\n}',['useCases'=>['Database connection handling','File operation error recovery','API request failure handling','Input validation with custom errors'],['mistakes'=>['Catching generic Exception only','Swallowing exceptions silently','Not using finally for cleanup'],['tips'=>['Catch specific exceptions first','Always clean up in finally','Log exceptions in catch blocks'],'interview'=>['When to use try-catch?','Exception vs Error in PHP 7?','How to create custom exceptions?']],
['name'=>'Custom Exceptions','brief'=>'Creating exception classes','explanation':'Create custom exceptions by extending Exception. Add custom properties and methods. Useful for distinguishing different error types in your application. Override __toString for custom formatting.','syntax'=>'<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">AppException</span> <span class="kw">extends</span> <span class="fn">Exception</span> {\n    <span class="kw">private</span> <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$code</span>;\n\n    <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">__construct</span>(\n        <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$message</span>,\n        <span class="var">string</span> <span class="var">$code</span>\n    ) {\n        <span class="kw">parent</span>::<span class="fn">__construct</span>(<span class="var">$message</span>);\n        <span class="var">$this</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="var">code</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$code</span>;\n    }\n\n    <span class="kw">public</span> <span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">getCode</span>(): <span class="var">string</span> {\n        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="var">$this</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="var">code</span>;\n    }\n}','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">UserNotFoundException</span> <span class="kw">extends</span> <span class="fn">RuntimeException</span> {}\n<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">InvalidEmailException</span> <span class="kw">extends</span> <span class="fn">InvalidArgumentException</span> {}\n\n<span class="kw">function</span> <span class="fn">findUser</span>(<span class="kw">int</span> <span class="var">$id</span>): <span class="var">array</span> {\n    <span class="cmt">// simulate DB lookup</span>\n    <span class="kw">throw new</span> <span class="fn">UserNotFoundException</span>(\n        <span class="str">"User #</span><span class="var">$id</span><span class="str"> not found"</span>\n    );\n}\n\n<span class="kw">try</span> {\n    <span class="var">$user</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">findUser</span>(<span class="num">999</span>);\n} <span class="kw">catch</span> (<span class="fn">UserNotFoundException</span> <span class="var">$e</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Not found: </span><span class="var">$e-&gt;getMessage()</span><span class="str">"</span>;\n} <span class="kw">catch</span> (<span class="fn">Exception</span> <span class="var">$e</span>) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="str">"Other error"</span>;\n}',['useCases'=>['Distinguishing error types','Domain-specific error handling','API error responses','Validation error reporting'],['mistakes'=>['Extending Exception instead of RuntimeException','Not including useful context in messages','Catching too broadly'],['tips'=>['Extend RuntimeException for runtime errors','Include context data in exceptions','Use multiple catch blocks for different types'],'interview'=>['How to create custom exceptions?','Exception vs RuntimeException?','Best practices for exception handling?']]
]
