'id'=>'database','name'=>'Database','icon'=>'🗄️','color'=>'#10b981',
'subs'=>[
['name'=>'MySQLi','brief'=>'MySQL Improved extension','explanation'=>'MySQLi supports procedural and OOP interfaces with prepared statements and transactions. Always use prepared statements to prevent SQL injection.','syntax'=>'<span class="var">$db</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">mysqli</span>(<span class="str">\'host\'</span>,<span class="str">\'user\'</span>,<span class="str">\'pass\'</span>,<span class="str">\'db\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$db</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=?"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">bind_param</span>(<span class="str">"i"</span>,<span class="var">$id</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>();','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$db</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">mysqli</span>(<span class="str">\'localhost\'</span>,<span class="str">\'root\'</span>,<span class="str">\'\'</span>,<span class="str">\'mydb\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$db</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">query</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users LIMIT 5"</span>);\n<span class="kw">while</span> (<span class="var">$row</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$result</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">fetch_assoc</span>()) {\n    <span class="kw">echo</span> <span class="var">$row</span>[<span class="str">\'name\'</span>] <span class="op">.</span> <span class="str">"&lt;br&gt;"</span>;\n}\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$db</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"INSERT INTO users (name,email) VALUES (?,?)"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">bind_param</span>(<span class="str">"ss"</span>,<span class="var">$name</span>,<span class="var">$email</span>);\n<span class="var">$name</span>=<span class="str">"Alice"</span>; <span class="var">$email</span>=<span class="str">"a@b.com"</span>;\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>();','useCases'=>['Web application storage','Content management','E-commerce catalogs','User management'],['mistakes'=>['SQL injection without prepared statements','Not closing connections','Not handling query errors'],['tips'=>['Always use prepared statements','Use transactions for related operations','Close connections when done'],'interview'=>['How to prevent SQL injection?','MySQLi vs PDO?','What are prepared statements?']],
['name'=>'PDO','brief'=>'PHP Data Objects abstraction','explanation'=>'PDO provides a consistent interface for multiple databases. Supports prepared statements, transactions, and multiple fetch modes. More flexible than MySQLi.','syntax'=>'<span class="var">$pdo</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">PDO</span>(<span class="str">"mysql:host=localhost;dbname=mydb"</span>,<span class="str">\'user\'</span>,<span class="str">\'pass\'</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=:email"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="str">\'email\'</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="str">\'a@b.com\'</span>]);','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="var">$pdo</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="fn">PDO</span>(<span class="str">"mysql:host=localhost;dbname=mydb;charset=utf8"</span>,<span class="str">\'root\'</span>,<span class="str">\'\'</span>,[\n    <span class="const">PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE</span> <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="const">PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION</span>\n]);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=:email"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="str">\'email\'</span> <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="str">\'a@b.com\'</span>]);\n<span class="var">$user</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">fetch</span>(<span class="const">PDO::FETCH_ASSOC</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"INSERT INTO users (name,email) VALUES (?,?)"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="str">\'Alice\'</span>,<span class="str">\'a@b.com\'</span>]);','useCases'=>['Multi-database apps','Database abstraction','Complex queries','Transactions'],['mistakes'=>['Not setting ERRMODE_EXCEPTION','String concatenation for queries','Not closing cursor'],['tips'=>['Use named parameters','Set error mode to exception','Use fetchAll for small results'],'interview'=>['PDO vs MySQLi?','Why prepared statements?','PDO fetch modes?']],
['name'=>'CRUD Operations','brief'=>'Create, Read, Update, Delete','explanation':'CRUD represents the four basic database operations. Every data-driven application needs these implemented securely with prepared statements.','syntax'=>'<span class="cmt">// CREATE</span>\n$stmt->execute([\'Alice\',\'a@b.com\']);\n<span class="cmt">// READ</span>\n$rows = $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);\n<span class="cmt">// UPDATE</span>\n$stmt = $pdo->prepare("UPDATE users SET name=? WHERE id=?");\n<span class="cmt">// DELETE</span>\n$stmt = $pdo->prepare("DELETE FROM users WHERE id=?");','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// CREATE</span>\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"INSERT INTO users (name,email) VALUES (?,?)"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="str">\'Alice\'</span>,<span class="str">\'alice@b.com\'</span>]);\n<span class="cmt">// READ</span>\n<span class="var">$users</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">query</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users"</span>)-><span class="fn">fetchAll</span>(<span class="const">PDO::FETCH_ASSOC</span>);\n<span class="cmt">// UPDATE</span>\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"UPDATE users SET name=? WHERE id=?"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="str">\'Bob\'</span>,<span class="num">1</span>]);\n<span class="cmt">// DELETE</span>\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"DELETE FROM users WHERE id=?"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="num">1</span>]);','useCases'=>['User management','Content management','Product catalogs','Blog systems'],['mistakes'=>['SQL injection','Missing WHERE on UPDATE/DELETE','No transactions for related ops'],['tips'=>['Always use prepared statements','Use transactions for multi-table ops','Always include WHERE clause'],'interview'=>['What does CRUD mean?','Why use transactions?','How to handle large results?']],
['name'=>'Prepared Statements','brief'=>'Preventing SQL injection','explanation':'Prepared statements separate SQL from data. SQL is prepared with placeholders, then data is bound. Prevents injection because input is never treated as SQL code.','syntax'=>'<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=:email"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="str">\'email\'</span><span class="op">=&gt;</span><span class="var">$email</span>]);\n<span class="var">$user</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">fetch</span>();','codeExample'=>'<span class="op">&lt;?</span><span class="kw">php</span>\n<span class="cmt">// DANGEROUS - never do this!</span>\n<span class="cmt">// $db->query("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=\'$email\'");</span>\n\n<span class="cmt">// SAFE - prepared statement</span>\n<span class="var">$email</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$_POST</span>[<span class="str">\'email\'</span>];\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email=:email"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>([<span class="str">\'email\'</span> <span class="op">=&gt;</span> <span class="var">$email</span>]);\n<span class="var">$user</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">fetch</span>();\n\n<span class="cmt">// IN clause</span>\n<span class="var">$ids</span> <span class="op">=</span> [<span class="num">1</span>,<span class="num">2</span>,<span class="num">3</span>];\n<span class="var">$ph</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">implode</span>(<span class="str">\',\'</span>,<span class="fn">array_fill</span>(<span class="num">0</span>,<span class="fn">count</span>(<span class="var">$ids</span>),<span class="str">\'?\'</span>));\n<span class="var">$stmt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="var">$pdo</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">prepare</span>(<span class="str">"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id IN (</span><span class="var">$ph</span><span class="str">)"</span>);\n<span class="var">$stmt</span><span class="op">-&gt;</span><span class="fn">execute</span>(<span class="var">$ids</span>);','useCases'=>['All queries with user input','Search functionality','Dynamic WHERE clauses','Bulk IN operations'],['mistakes'=>['String concatenation for queries','Not using prepared statements','Forgetting to bind parameters'],['tips'=>['Always use prepared statements','Use named params for readability','Pre-prepare when possible'],'interview'=>['What is SQL injection?','How do prepared statements prevent it?','Named vs positional params?']]
]
